WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.535
-My first guest
is a legendary performer

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.771
and one of the biggest stars
on the planet.

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:07.573
He's a multiple award-winning
actor and comedian

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:10.276
that's been making us laugh
for the past 40 years.

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:14.380
His highly anticipated sequel
"Coming 2 America"

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:18.418
is available on Amazon
Prime Video on March 5th,

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:19.852
next Friday, March 5th.

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:22.655
It is going break
Amazon Prime Video.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.023
That's how funny this thing is.

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:26.525
Here he is, Eddie Murphy!

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:27.961
Eddie, thank you so much.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.428
-Hey, what's going on, man?

00:00:29.428 --> 00:00:30.730
Thanks for having me.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.932
-Ah, are you kidding me?
I always love having you here.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.166
I appreciate this.

00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:36.102
The last time
you were on our show

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.670
was a little over a year ago

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.939
when we had people
in the audience,

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.508
and you were hosting
"Saturday Night Live"

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:44.310
for the first time in 35 years.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.578
-Yeah.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:48.280
-And you knocked it
out of the park! I loved it!

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.485
-Yeah, that was a great
show-business moment for me.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:56.355
To go back to the show and have
the show be as good as it was

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:58.491
and for so many people tune in,

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:01.994
that was a great
show-business moment for me.

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:03.696
-For everybody.
Everyone needed --

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.965
It was just so perfect,
and it was funny,

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.701
and you won an Emmy.
Congratulations for that.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.971
-Oh, yeah, yeah.
That was the cherry on top.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.940
-Yeah, that was the extra jam,
'cause you go,

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.875
"Wow, I'm just doing this
for fun."

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.077
-That was like, you know,
winning the basketball game

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:22.081
at the buzzer by dunking
and you shatter the backboard.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:23.616
-[ Laughing ] Yeah. Oh, my God.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:26.085
-Yeah. Then they lift you up.
-It was a moment like that.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.887
-They lift you up, yeah.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:31.724
What was it like
going back to Studio 8H and --

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.293
What was your memory?
Were you like, "Oh yeah --"

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:35.195
What was the night like?

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:36.829
-It was surreal. It was surreal.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:40.132
And I was tripping of off
how it's the exact same --

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:41.501
You know, it's the same --

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.671
They've been doing that show
the same way for 45 years.

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.105
It's a trip.

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:48.140
The exact same way.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.843
So it was a trip. It was like
going back to high school

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.745
and them giving you
your old schedule.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.647
and be like, "Okay,
I have lunch at this today.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.015
I got science at 12:00."

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.217
That's what it was like.

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:59.919
But it was bunch of
new students, though.

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:03.289
You sit in your old classroom
and look at my old locker.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.091
It was that kind of --
-It was so good.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:07.694
Congrats on that.
I just loved every single thing.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.662
Honestly, I was nerding out.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.797
And it was just well done.

00:02:11.797 --> 00:02:14.166
It was just
a home run, home run.

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:17.703
Speaking of home runs, I got to
talk about "Coming 2 America."

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:20.473
The sequel is something
that people have been wanting

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:23.776
since the first one
came out in 1988.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.678
Why was now the right time?

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.780
How did you know to do it now?

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.882
-We never thought about
doing a sequel to the movie.

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:31.050
We thought it was over,

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.752
'cause the story ended
with him going off.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.720
It looked like they was going
to live happily ever after,

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.322
and that was
the end of the story.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:39.692
And then the movie became
this cult movie, like, you know,

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:42.195
of all the movies that I've
done, "Coming to America"

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:45.398
is the one that like worked
its way into the culture

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:46.499
in all these different ways,

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:49.068
little catchphrases
from the movie.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:53.706
Quest used to have a band called
"The Randy Watson Experience."

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.975
Questlove. He did.
He used to have a little --

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:58.144
So it's like you have
stuff like that.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:02.481
And you have, like, on
Halloween, people get dressed up

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:05.217
as characters from
"Coming to America."

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:08.254
There's a restaurant
in New York -- I mean in L.A.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:11.991
that on Halloween changed itself
into McDowell's Restaurant.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:16.495
And they have, like, Sexual
Chocolate milkshakes and stuff.

00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:19.498
So it was like, yo, this movie's
like a cult movie, you know.

00:03:19.498 --> 00:03:20.667
So I was like, "Yo."

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:23.236
So, it took 25 years
for it to become that.

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:25.738
Then I started to, you know,
thinking, "Hey, if I could

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:29.141
figure out a way
to connect those dots,

00:03:29.141 --> 00:03:30.609
we could do a sequel
to those movies."

00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:33.079
And I got an idea, and it all
kind of came together.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:35.448
-Can you set up for everyone
where the sequel picks up?

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:37.683
-The sequel picks up
30 years later,

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:42.488
and we're right in the middle
of our happily ever after,

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:48.794
and then we have to deal
with a very modern problem.

00:03:48.794 --> 00:03:50.229
[ Laughs ]

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:54.067
Our fairy tale is disrupted
by a very modern problem.

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.235
-Mm-hmm. Yep. Exactly right.

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:58.638
It is so beyond funny.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:02.174
I want to -- I mean, just crush.
I mean, just crush.

00:04:02.174 --> 00:04:04.844
You doing all your characters.

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:08.414
The barbershop crew is back.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:11.117
Arsenio doing
the other characters.

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:13.085
Leslie Jones, by the way --

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:15.454
Wow.
-Leslie Jones, Leslie Jones,

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:19.224
talk about -- Leslie Jones
in this movie is insane.

00:04:19.224 --> 00:04:20.360
-I mean, everyone's home
right now.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:23.029
We need something funny.
It is so funny.

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:25.264
-Nice. It's funny, light, funny,

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:27.165
put a little smile
on your heart.

00:04:27.165 --> 00:04:28.834
It's a nice little movie.

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:30.169
I'm so proud of it.

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:32.438
-And the spoilers -- I don't
want to spoil everything,

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:34.706
but Wesley Snipes.

00:04:34.706 --> 00:04:36.208
-Wesley Snipes.

00:04:36.208 --> 00:04:38.344
I had just did --

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.646
Last year, I did
"Dolemite is my Name"

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:42.014
with Wesley Snipes.

00:04:42.014 --> 00:04:46.619
And we had such an incredible
time making that film

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:49.455
and had just such strong
screen chemistry,

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.423
I just wanted to work with him
right again.

00:04:51.423 --> 00:04:52.658
We went right into this.

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:54.393
The role that he's playing
in the movie,

00:04:54.393 --> 00:04:57.396
originally, I was supposed
to play the General Izzi.

00:04:57.396 --> 00:04:59.231
I was supposed to be
the General Izzi,

00:04:59.231 --> 00:05:01.033
and I was supposed to be
the witch doctor,

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:03.302
and it was like,

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:06.072
Wesley would be so much better
in that role than me,

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:08.641
'cause Wesley can be menacing.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.842
If I would have been
the General,

00:05:10.842 --> 00:05:13.312
I would have just been funny,
and it would have been me

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:15.214
being threatened
by one of my characters.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:16.482
It wouldn't have been the same.

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:18.918
But Wesley brought
this whole other [bleep] to it

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:22.188
and just jumped off the screen.
-He's menacing but funny.

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:23.723
-And funny, yeah.

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:28.627
You know, people forgot about
that Wesley could do everything.

00:05:28.627 --> 00:05:31.931
'Cause Wesley became famous
for doing them action movies

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:33.800
and became this big action star,

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:37.536
people forgot
that Wesley can do drama.

00:05:37.536 --> 00:05:41.206
Wesley can do comedy.
Wesley can do action, movies.

00:05:41.206 --> 00:05:43.642
-"White Men Can't Jump."

00:05:43.642 --> 00:05:45.711
-Yeah, -"White Men Can't Jump,"
"To Wong Foo."

00:05:45.711 --> 00:05:48.214
Wesley is the great
Wesley Snipes.

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:50.349
The great Wesley Snipes, yo.

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:52.684
Yeah, he crushed this movie.

00:05:52.684 --> 00:05:56.989
-And I have to -- Randy Watson,
Sexual Chocolate.

00:05:56.989 --> 00:06:00.193
-That's my favorite
of all the characters to do

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:01.327
is Randy Watson.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:02.862
If I could figure out a way

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:06.165
to do a whole Randy Watson
movie, I would do it.

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:08.400
He's a funny character.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.135
-The mic drop.

00:06:10.135 --> 00:06:12.137
I've seen this on the Internet.

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:14.172
There's a debate.
There's something going around.

00:06:14.172 --> 00:06:18.477
People say that that is
the very first-ever mic drop

00:06:18.477 --> 00:06:19.845
in the history of pop culture.

00:06:19.845 --> 00:06:21.881
-Yeah, I don't know what anyone
is debating about,

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.849
'cause I heard somebody say --

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:26.318
Somebody was like, "Oh,
it started with the rappers."

00:06:26.318 --> 00:06:30.823
The very first mic drop ever,
ever, where it's like,

00:06:30.823 --> 00:06:34.193
what I said was so --
you know, so fly,

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:36.462
there's nothing left to say,
and I'm dropping the mic,

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:37.630
that's Randy Watson.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.398
Now, in 1983,

00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:42.268
at the end of "Delirious,"
I threw my mic down

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:44.870
and it slid down to the ground,
but that wasn't a mic drop.

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:47.306
I said, "Thank you. Good night."
I throw the mic down cool.

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:49.909
It wasn't like a, you know,
I crushed and dropped.

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:53.879
The very first one to do that
is Randy Watson.

00:06:53.879 --> 00:06:55.547
-Wow.
-And I defy anyone

00:06:55.547 --> 00:06:59.017
to find any footage of anyone
doing that before Randy Watson.

00:06:59.017 --> 00:07:00.286
-Yeah, I agree.

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:02.521
What was it, Whitney Houston,
what did he sing?

00:07:02.521 --> 00:07:03.822
He sang --

00:07:03.822 --> 00:07:06.024
Why did he drop the mic, again?

00:07:06.024 --> 00:07:08.660
-Yeah, he was --
"The Greatest Love of All."

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:10.162
-"Greatest Love of All."

00:07:10.162 --> 00:07:13.565
-And he crushed it and dropped
the mic at the end of it.

00:07:13.565 --> 00:07:14.800
-Oh, my gosh.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:17.503
-And you know what?
That was improvised.

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:19.405
That was an improvised moment,

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:22.741
and the name of the band,
Sexual Chocolate,

00:07:22.741 --> 00:07:25.177
that night,
I must have said 10 --

00:07:25.177 --> 00:07:27.780
Every take, I would say
a different name to the band.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.148
"This is my band So and So."

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:31.183
And it would just get
more and more ridiculous.

00:07:31.183 --> 00:07:33.285
Then that was the ridiculous one
that stayed in.

00:07:33.285 --> 00:07:35.421
But somewhere, there's
all these other names

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:36.823
of that band that night.

00:07:36.823 --> 00:07:38.791
-Sexual Chocolate.
I'm telling you --

00:07:38.791 --> 00:07:40.292
-Sexual Chocolate is insane.

00:07:40.292 --> 00:07:43.295
-That is the dumbest name
I've ever heard in my entire --

00:07:43.295 --> 00:07:47.033
-[ Laughs ]
-It's levels of funny.

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:48.467
It's levels.

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:51.336
But you know, someone should
make a real Sexual Chocolate.

00:07:51.336 --> 00:07:54.307
Just call the Willy Wonka people
or whoever makes chocolate bars,

00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:55.374
Hershey's or whatever it is.

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:57.042
-Amazon did this cool thing,

00:07:57.042 --> 00:08:00.879
promotion for this film
on Valentine's Day.

00:08:00.879 --> 00:08:03.015
They sent out
all these chocolates

00:08:03.015 --> 00:08:04.917
with Randy Watson's
picture on it.

00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:07.252
It was Randy Watson's
Sexual Chocolates.

00:08:07.252 --> 00:08:10.423
There was a picture of Randy
singing to the chocolate.

00:08:10.423 --> 00:08:12.224
It was hysterical.

00:08:12.224 --> 00:08:14.093
-I want to show a clip

00:08:14.093 --> 00:08:16.762
and hopefully --
It doesn't even do the film --

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:18.297
I'm telling you,
if you want to laugh --

00:08:18.297 --> 00:08:20.332
Everyone needs
a laugh right now.

00:08:20.332 --> 00:08:22.768
If you want some heart,
just get together

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:25.937
with whoever you can in your pod
or whatever you can do,

00:08:25.937 --> 00:08:28.274
call somebody and say,
"Let's start it at this time."

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:30.710
You will love this movie.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:33.379
Here's Eddie Murphy
in "Coming 2 America."

00:08:33.379 --> 00:08:34.847
Take a look.

00:08:34.847 --> 00:08:38.618
-Soon, Nextdoorian warriors
will assassinate me.

00:08:38.618 --> 00:08:42.554
I have a child on the other side
of the world.

00:08:42.554 --> 00:08:45.558
-Take heart in your grief.
You are King now.

00:08:45.558 --> 00:08:47.059
Be as your father.

00:08:47.059 --> 00:08:49.562
Bark orders at me.
Throw things at me.

00:08:49.562 --> 00:08:51.898
It will make you happy.

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:59.772
-Prepare the royal jet.

00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:03.709
We are going back to America.

00:09:03.709 --> 00:09:06.111
-Oh, hell no, Your Majesty.

00:09:06.111 --> 00:09:08.514
-More with Eddie Murphy
when we come back, everybody.

